# Plasma desktop applet layout (railjack).
#
# INTENTIONALLY IMMUTABLE. Home Manager force-writes this file on every
# activation, so anything Plasma changes at runtime (a rearranged panel, a new
# desktop icon, a monitor being plugged in) is reverted at the next login. That
# is deliberate: this file is the source of truth for the panel contents, the
# launcher ids and the wallpaper, and it keeps the desktop identical across
# rebuilds. Anything that should survive an activation belongs here, not in the
# live Plasma config.
#
# Notes for editing:
#   * Containments 1 + 2 are screen 0, 72 + 73 are screen 1. The second pair is
#     not a duplicate of the first, it is the second monitor's panel and desktop
#     folder; deleting either pair removes that screen's desktop.
#   * The activityId below is the live activity UUID, not a placeholder. Change
#     it and Plasma creates a new activity and renumbers the activities.
#   * ScreenMapping is rewritten by Plasma whenever the monitor set changes; it
#     has to be regenerated from the next live configuration.
#   * The wallpaper is the single file below. SlidePaths keeps Breeze's "Next"
#     wallpaper (the only thing left in that directory, since
#     plasma-workspace-wallpapers is excluded system-wide) as slideshow source.
#
# Pinned launchers use real XDG desktop ids instead of preferred://filemanager /
# preferred://browser, which never resolve on NixOS (there is no kde-defaults /
# kcm_defaultapps provider there, so the panel rendered blank "ghost" icons).
# Everything else is carried over verbatim from the previous live configuration.
